@startuml ViaMe_StateRide
title State Machine — Ride lifecycle

skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #FDF6E3
  BorderColor #333333
  ArrowColor #333333
}

[*] --> REQUESTED : passenger confirms

REQUESTED --> ASSIGNED         : driver offered & accepted
REQUESTED --> NO_DRIVER_FOUND  : no candidate / 3 rejections
REQUESTED --> CANCELLED        : passenger cancels (free)

ASSIGNED --> DRIVER_EN_ROUTE   : driver accepts
ASSIGNED --> REQUESTED         : driver rejects / timeout
ASSIGNED --> CANCELLED         : cancel (fee applies)

DRIVER_EN_ROUTE --> ARRIVED    : driver at pickup
DRIVER_EN_ROUTE --> CANCELLED  : cancel (fee applies)

ARRIVED --> IN_PROGRESS        : driver starts trip
ARRIVED --> CANCELLED          : passenger no-show (fee applies)

IN_PROGRESS --> COMPLETED      : driver completes
IN_PROGRESS --> CANCELLED      : emergency cancel

COMPLETED        --> [*]
CANCELLED        --> [*]
NO_DRIVER_FOUND  --> [*]

note right of ASSIGNED
  Every transition is validated server-side
  (RideService). Illegal transitions throw
  IllegalStateTransitionException.
end note

note right of ASSIGNED
  Optimistic lock on `version`
  guards double assignment.
end note

@enduml
